{"name":"Limoncello","hex":"#bfff00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limoncello","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of Italian lemon-flavoured liqueur.","A glass of this drink."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limoncello"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limoncello","blocks":[{"text":"Limoncello is a traditional lemon liqueur produced mainly in Southern Italy, especially around the Gulf of Naples, the Gulf of Salerno, as well as in Sicily and in Gargano. It is the second-most popular liqueur in Italy and is traditionally served chilled as an after-dinner digestif. It is also a popular homemade liqueur, with various recipes available online and in print."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limoncello","wikidata":"Q736208"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Homemade_limoncello.jpg/500px-Homemade_limoncello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Homemade_limoncello.jpg/500px-Homemade_limoncello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomemade_limoncello.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/P1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg/500px-P1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/P1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg/1280px-P1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/P1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg/500px-P1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Limoncello","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AP1160657-Limoncello_di_Ravello.jpg"}